# What: Sample HTTP requests for the attachments sample (VS Code "REST Client" / IntelliJ HTTP client).
# Why: [CAP-M15] the two-step upload (metadata, then bytes) and the download, clickable.
# If missing or unlinked: Learners have to reconstruct media URLs from the tests.
#
# Start first: npm run watch. Copy the ID from request 1 into @doc.

@P = http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/documents

### 1 Create the document (metadata only)
POST {{P}}/Documents
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Quote Bürotec", "fileName": "quote.txt" }

### 2 Upload the bytes
@doc = replace-with-ID-from-request-1
PUT {{P}}/Documents({{doc}})/content
Content-Type: text/plain

Quote: 4 office chairs, 759.60 EUR

### 3 Download - note Content-Type and Content-Disposition
GET {{P}}/Documents({{doc}})/content

### 4 Metadata incl. size - no bytes in the JSON
GET {{P}}/Documents({{doc}})

### 5 Not allowed -> 415
PUT {{P}}/Documents({{doc}})/content
Content-Type: application/x-msdownload

MZ
